>> title: Meatloaf
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, pork, baked, southern, glaze
>> counters: Meat and Three, Diner
>> aka: meat loaf, glazed meatloaf, ketchup-glazed meatloaf, meatloaf plate
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 45 min
>> slack: unforgiving — ground meat is not a cut of meat and the middle has to reach temperature, which is what the hour is for; the mixing is the other end of it, because a loaf worked past just-combined bakes dense and springy and no amount of glaze redeems that
>> pairs-with: cream-gravy, macaroni-and-cheese, green-beans, stewed-squash
>> step.1: Bake it free-form on a sheet pan rather than in a loaf tin. A tin steams the sides and gives the fat nowhere to go; on a flat pan the whole outside browns and the glaze sets rather than pooling.
>> step.2: soak the bread 10 min
>> step.3: sweat 8 min, then cool
>> step.4: mix by hand, lightly
>> step.5: shape into a loaf
>> step.6: glaze, bake 350°F 1 hr

Bake it free-form on a sheet pan rather than in a loaf tin. A tin steams the sides and gives the fat nowhere to go; on a flat pan the whole outside browns and the glaze sets rather than pooling.

Soak @white sandwich bread{3%slices}(torn) in @whole milk{3/4%cup}(180 mL) for ~soak{10%min}.

Sweat @yellow onion{1%large}(finely diced), @celery{2%ribs}(finely diced), @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) for ~sweat{8%min}.

Mix @&(~2)soaked bread{}, @&(~1)cooled vegetables{} with @ground beef{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; 80/20), @ground pork{1/2%lb}(225 g), @large eggs{2}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%Tbs}.

Shape @&(~1)meatloaf mixture{} into a loaf on a #sheet pan{}, no taller than three inches.

Bake @&(~1)shaped loaf{} at 350°F (175°C) under @ketchup{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @light brown sugar{2%Tbs}(25 g), @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} for ~bake{60%min}.

Rest the loaf ten minutes before it is cut. Sliced straight out of the oven it falls apart on the spatula, and a meat-and-three plate is served in slices rather than in pieces.
